{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/914553-help-with-simplified-templates-for-players","id":914553,"title":"Help With Simplified Templates for Players","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-14T18:56:35-07:00","id":914553,"title":"Help With Simplified Templates for Players","content":"Hello!<br /> <br /> We tried to play with simplified templates in a mixed party, based in some NPC ideas in the Hunter's handbook (like vampires in NightStalkers, werewolves in SpiritSlayers and Witches in Witchfinders) but it was a DISASTER.<br /> <br /> The reason for that is even you adjust the XP cost t\u00f4 acquire each new trait, it is not balanced for players. For example, blood potency and primal urge in the Requiem and Forsaken CoreBook, respect the same schedule about energy consumption/turn and Max dot/dot of power trait.<br /> But in the Hunter's hamdbook, this doesn't happens. The Vampire with Blood Potency 5(that now is a Merit) can increase attributes to 10, but werewolves with Primal, doesn't. And what the cost of this Blood Potency, if with 5 dots only you can increase traits to 10??<br /> <br /> But looking to other side, i don't think that have sense read all 350 pages from vampires and/or 350 pages from werewolves and/or 400 pages from mages (and the others templates) just to make ONE character. I guess these CoreBooks about templates is good to play a entire campaign-based on that creatures, but not in a mixed one.<br /> <br /> What is your experience in a scenario with players with mixed templates? How do you deal with it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9723,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9723-winchester","user":"winchester","date":". 06-14-2016, 09:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9723-winchester","name":"winchester","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T19:04:53-07:00","id":914561,"title":"","content":"I don't bother trying to do it, generally. <br /> <br /> Pick one game and stick with it; Changeling tends to do this best. That way, your Werewolf player can make a Hunterheart Beast and your Vampire player can make a Leechfinger Darkling and everybody goes home happy without the poor ST having to houserule everything or juggle crazy balance on the fly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T05:10:33-07:00","id":914757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/914553-help-with-simplified-templates-for-players?p=914561#post914561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't bother trying to do it, generally. <br /> <br /> Pick one game and stick with it; Changeling tends to do this best. That way, your Werewolf player can make a Hunterheart Beast and your Vampire player can make a Leechfinger Darkling and everybody goes home happy without the poor ST having to houserule everything or juggle crazy balance on the fly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, just Changeling? All the Core books, this is the one that i never checked. Kkkkkk<br /> <br /> But this was what I really did, but using Hunter, picking one game and using it. But that monsters NPCs really don't work for players.<br /> <br /> Changeling is simplified?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9723-winchester","name":"winchester","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T05:53:41-07:00","id":914773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>winchester</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/914553-help-with-simplified-templates-for-players?p=914757#post914757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changeling is simplified?</div> </div> </div> </div>no, he meant that with the combination of seeming and kith (and there are DOZENS) in changeling you have enough material to reskin lots of monsters, with many minor, interesting abilities. A leechfinger isn't a requiem vampire or masquerade Cainite, but it's a passable generic vampire for whatever cosmology you are playing. Need a bigfoot? Choose some ogre seeming and you're set. That strange being that removes people's kidneys while they are sleeping? There's a kith with medical equipment as fingers IIRC.<br /> <br /> You don't need to use them as changeling or even fey-related since it's pretty easy to reskin anything as a GM. If I say that the bloodsucker is actually a plutonium zombie then it is, and changeling gives you lots of options. For example you could use the kiths as the many &quot;races&quot; of a fantasy setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11854,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11854-dibastet","user":"DiBastet","date":". 06-15-2016, 08:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11854-dibastet","name":"DiBastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T19:37:26-07:00","id":915297,"title":"","content":"Because somethings confuse me. For example, if a character want to do a werewolf, between the books we have the Uratha Werewolf, Skinchangers and Changing Breeds. Truly, I don't know how template to use. I know the traits changes, but the concept between then is very similar for me. And the rules isn't so integrated to use both in the same story and for me, sounds strange. &quot;uh, i'm a werewolf that can use Gifts to cause aggravatted damage. Oh, my char is a werewolf too, but I'm using skinchangers I just have Aspects. And my is a Breed Werewolf, that doesn't have the Hybrid form...&quot; Wtf??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9723-winchester","name":"winchester","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T19:39:22-07:00","id":915300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>winchester</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/914553-help-with-simplified-templates-for-players?p=915297#post915297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because somethings confuse me. For example, if a character want to do a werewolf, between the books we have the Uratha Werewolf, Skinchangers and Changing Breeds. Truly, I don't know how template to use. I know the traits changes, but the concept between then is very similar for me. And the rules isn't so integrated to use both in the same story and for me, sounds strange. &amp;quot;uh, i'm a werewolf that can use Gifts to cause aggravatted damage. Oh, my char is a werewolf too, but I'm using skinchangers I just have Aspects. And my is a Breed Werewolf, that doesn't have the Hybrid form...&amp;quot; Wtf??</div> </div> </div> </div>You solve this problem by choosing one game and sticking to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T19:57:22-07:00","id":915310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>winchester</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/914553-help-with-simplified-templates-for-players?p=915297#post915297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the rules isn't so integrated to use both in the same story and for me, sounds strange.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't treat it as if it was some integrated canon world. It's a toolbox that you can choose pieces from to tell a story. Modern horror with werebeast as virus? Works. As a witch curse? Works as well. Both? Interesting, so sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11854-dibastet","name":"DiBastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T20:10:59-07:00","id":915322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/914553-help-with-simplified-templates-for-players?p=915300#post915300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You solve this problem by choosing one game and sticking to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Choosing one game and sticking that you said is a good point. I guess i did the wrong question. Let me tell you what causes this.<br /> <br /> We are playing a campaign about Hunters (using Hunter the vigil, of course). But some players wanted something different from a human character and its conspiracies, they wanted to add some supernatural templates to character. But in the core, he is still a Hunter, with supernatural Powers that maybe corrupt him, maybe the time will Tell. This is the theme.<br /> <br /> But how to add a supernatural template in a Hunter The Vigil character? We tried to use Dread Powers, because this seems simplified, easy and there is no need to read another core books for understanding. But the game doesn't define XP to balance this Powers. So, when se tried to do that, something goes wrong. The werewolf or vampire or whatever with a few XP could acquire the most dangerous Dread Powers easily. Was not balanced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9723,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9723-winchester","user":"winchester","date":". 06-15-2016, 11:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9723-winchester","name":"winchester","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T20:46:06-07:00","id":915344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>winchester</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/914553-help-with-simplified-templates-for-players?p=915322#post915322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Choosing one game and sticking that you said is a good point. I guess i did the wrong question. Let me tell you what causes this.<br /> <br /> We are playing a campaign about Hunters (using Hunter the vigil, of course). But some players wanted something different from a human character and its conspiracies, they wanted to add some supernatural templates to character. But in the core, he is still a Hunter, with supernatural Powers that maybe corrupt him, maybe the time will Tell. This is the theme.<br /> <br /> But how to add a supernatural template in a Hunter The Vigil character? We tried to use Dread Powers, because this seems simplified, easy and there is no need to read another core books for understanding. But the game doesn't define XP to balance this Powers. So, when se tried to do that, something goes wrong. The werewolf or vampire or whatever with a few XP could acquire the most dangerous Dread Powers easily. Was not balanced.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because those Dread Powers are aimed at building monsters for them to encounter, not for player use. If your player wants more than what Hunter offers by default he should first consider making a character that better fits Hunter's scale and scope, and then maybe look into &quot;blue books&quot; like Second Sight, which provides rules for mortal psychics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T05:42:35-07:00","id":915538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>winchester</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/914553-help-with-simplified-templates-for-players#post914553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We tried to play with simplified templates in a mixed party, based in some NPC ideas in the Hunter's handbook (like vampires in NightStalkers, werewolves in SpiritSlayers and Witches in Witchfinders) but it was a DISASTER.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hah. I was actually thinking about doing this for a <i>Suicide Squad</i> inspired game. Taskforce VALKYRIE captures some monsters and puts cranial bombs in them, or threatens to destroy their phylacteries or whatever, then it's all &quot;<a href=\"https://youtu.be/-EuwFw-7ke0\" target=\"_blank\">Assemble Taskforce X</a>&quot;<br /> <br /> If you want to have your players be supernaturals but still only use Hunter rules, you'll have to do a lot more hands on stuff than usual. Here are my suggestions (I assume you have Mortal Remains):<ul><li>Treat Potency as an Attribute. So you buy it for 4 Experiences (or you can go 5, if you really want). Refluff Potency as desired. A Vampire has Blood Potency, a Werewolf has Primal Urge. A robot might have Engine. A Mummy might have Sekhem, but you're not playing <i>Mummy: The Curse</i>, you're playing Hunter, so maybe it's got something else.</li> <li>Instead of using Willpower, give everyone an Energy stat. Vitae (or Blood) for Vampires, Essence (or Rage) for Werewolves, Battery for Robots, Balance for Mummies, etcetera. Have them come up with their own term.</li> <li>Have everyone come up with some way to regain their Energy. A vampire might have to drink blood and gets 1 vitae per turn he deals 1L of damage. A werewolf might regain his Rage by running wild and hunting, or even eating flesh. A Robot's battery might require meditating under the sun or charging at a wall outlet (or punching a circuit breaker and regaining Battery based on how much damage is done to him). A Mummy might meditate on her canopic jars.</li> <li>Work to come up with a template for everyone. A vampire might not bleed, might take damage from sunlight, might downgrade all attacks due to having dead flesh, and might have the Drain Dread Power to represent how they feed. A Werewolf might have fast healing and the ability to transform by spending a point of Rage and rearrange their Attributes and get a Dread Attack. A Robot might have 2/2 armour and not need to breath or bleed or eat, but has to spend a point of Battery to stay active each day and has to be repaired because they can't heal. A Mummy might also be dead like a vampire. I don't know, Mummies are dumb.</li> <li>Worth it to also think of Banes or Bans they might have. Maybe your Vampire has a compulsion to count grains, or your Werewolf has hairy palms and a unibrow. Whatever your players think might be neat. They could even take it as a Persistent Condition acting as a Flaw. &quot;Photosensitive: You take a -3 penalty to all actions and need to spend one Blood every scene when in the sunlight; Beat: Your dislike of the sun causes you problems&quot; or so on.</li> <li>During actual play and as they spend Experiences, don't just let them take anything. Work with them to decide how they &quot;level up&quot;, and what Dread Powers they can take, and how those Dread Powers might work narratively and mechanically. Have them be bought at 2 Experiences per dot, or flat out 3 or 4 Experiences, if you feel treating them like Merits is too powerful.</li> <li>Feel free to completely ignore what the Power says. Some of the ones in Hunter and Mortal Remains are ranked, but the ranks don't do anything. Balefire could cost less and only do 2B damage. It could also be fluffed as, for instance, a robot's electrical field. Agonize could just be a flat Tilt that lasts as long as the monster does nothing else. Same for Confusion. Damnation, Dement, most of them, honestly. Just add Potency to the dice rolls. Maybe don't bother rolling Revivify. For Absorb Energy, maybe don't bother with a dot rating, and don't roll it. Actually, there are just a lot of Dread Powers where it's not really thematically appropriate to roll them, but then again it's good to have the roll and not need it than to wonder what you should roll and not have it. Keep the same method in mind when using the ones from the CofD core. You're the one making these dumb monsters your friends are playing, or at least, you're helping. You don't have to limit yourself to the book.</li> <li>Do you know some of the cool powers that &quot;Real&quot; Vampires/Werewolves/Faeries/whatever get? Well, feel free to copy them. Does your Robot want to be really strong? Unholy Attribute works, but maybe Vigor or Resilience is exactly what you're looking for.</li> </ul>The gist of it is that when you use Hunter only, you're going to have to do a <i>lot</i> of work. But honestly, I think it can be pretty rewarding. You're making your own monsters. Sure, the <s>World</s>Chronicles of Darkness covers one type of Vampire and Werewolf and Mages and Changelings and Prometheans and so on. But you get to make up your own. You get to decide what Vampires are like. Maybe you think that it would be interesting to have a Changeling that's the faerie baby left behind when the faerie steals a human. Maybe you want to play a monster story about being a robot, so you take Biomechanical Nightmare and Ghost in the Machine. Maybe you've got the Mixed Blessings or Miracle Dread Power that you can only use three times on someone else's behalf, and your monster is a Djinni. <br /> <br /> I've honestly thought a lot about this, and if I weren't setting up to run Mage 2e, I might pull the Suicide Squad idea off the back burner. I may push myself and run two games...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T07:06:25-07:00","id":915576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/914553-help-with-simplified-templates-for-players?p=915344#post915344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because those Dread Powers are aimed at building monsters for them to encounter, not for player use. If your player wants more than what Hunter offers by default he should first consider making a character that better fits Hunter's scale and scope, and then maybe look into &amp;quot;blue books&amp;quot; like Second Sight, which provides rules for mortal psychics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. But imagine the situation: a story that werewolf can spreads its curse, like lycantrophy and attacks an human player. Or Vampire wishes to turn one player his ghoul. Or can imagine another event that turns the player some kind of monster during the campaign. How do you deal with it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9723-winchester","name":"winchester","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T07:19:19-07:00","id":915584,"title":"","content":"Aspel, this seems a really good way to do. Like you said, maybe the problema is that i was considering things like power traits (primal, blood, gnosis) like Merits. So it was making the character the strongest of their specie with a few points of experiente.<br /> Comparing with other books, ALL of this traits costs dots x 8. And it is the base to calculate what is the most powerfull power you can get (a werewolf cannot get Gift more than its Primal, for example). Maybe this could work about the maximum Dread Power level.<br /> <br /> Another thing, this score goes 1 to 10. And in the 6\u00b0 dot, the character has a limit trait increased above 5. But in this level, the monster is so strongest that its difficult to live with him. Vampires cannot feed only humans blood anymore. Werewolves lost their Essence even without use. Its challenging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9723-winchester","name":"winchester","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T17:54:47-07:00","id":915942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>winchester</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/914553-help-with-simplified-templates-for-players?p=915576#post915576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure. But imagine the situation: a story that werewolf can spreads its curse, like lycantrophy and attacks an human player. Or Vampire wishes to turn one player his ghoul. Or can imagine another event that turns the player some kind of monster during the campaign. How do you deal with it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, there's an Elixir that turns you into a Vampire temporarily. If you Dramatically fail, you become a Vampire forever. Nehebkuah's Tears. It's great.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>winchester</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/914553-help-with-simplified-templates-for-players?p=915584#post915584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Comparing with other books, ALL of this traits costs dots x 8. And it is the base to calculate what is the most powerfull power you can get (a werewolf cannot get Gift more than its Primal, for example). Maybe this could work about the maximum Dread Power level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I actually assumed you were using 2e. A lot of the advice I gave miiiight be a little harder without Mortal Remains (which adds like 30 new Dread Powers, and has slightly more detailed template creation rules), though it's still doable.<br /> <br /> As for &quot;it becomes too hard to live&quot;, you've got to remember that you're playing Hunter, not Vampire or Werewolf. Monsters work however you want them to work. Plus, with Potency costing more than a merit dot, it becomes less incentivized to buy that up, even if you add Potency to power rolls or something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}